			<div class="content" id="post-content-1396897">
									

<p>I corrected a bit of math in the article (I assume this is a minor edit like correcting a typo, and thus does not require permission).</p>
<p>999^5 seconds would be 31,529,964 years, not 31,551,559 years.</p>
<p>999^5 = 995,009,990,004,999 seconds.<br />
995009990004999/60 = 16,583,499,833,416.65 minutes<br />
16583499833416.65/60 = 276,391,663,890.2775 hours<br />
276391663890.2775/24 = 11,516,319,328.7615625 days<br />
11516319328.7615625/365.25 ≈ 31,529,963.94 years</p>
<p>I think what happened is that you didn't account for leap day. It's still over thirty-one million years, though. On the other hand, it does change the rounded number from 31.6 million to 31.5 million.</p>

							</div>

								
