			<div class="content" id="post-content-1727171">
									

<p>Just nitpicking here, but I think the value the Foundation would use would differ from that slightly. According to the SI (which I assume the Foundation will follow because of scientific unambiguity) a year has, on average, 365.24219 SI days that consist of 86400 seconds each. So the amount of years should be, IMHO,</p>
<p>999^5/(86400*365.24219) ≈ 31,530,638 years</p>
<p>which makes a difference of approximately 674 years.</p>
<p>Also, I do realize the post I'm replying to is almost a year old but there are only two posts below this one in the entire comment section so replying to the actual discussion around the exact value seems to be the most obvious choice.</p>

